  "reason": "Blepharoplasty (CPT 15823) falls under the 'cosmetic' procedure category, which is explicitly excluded from coverage under the Meridian HMO Core plan. The clinical documentation also confirms a cosmetic indication (patient reports tired appearance, no functional complaint, full visual fields, and margin-to-reflex distance of 4mm bilaterally, which does not meet the functional/anatomic criteria for medically necessary blepharoplasty under MP-COS-001). Because the benefit category itself is excluded, the request cannot be authorized regardless of clinical findings.",
